WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.773
This video walks through a full install of the Copilot Center of Excellence kit in a GCC Moderate tenant.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:10.904
It is the same eight-step process used in production deployments.

00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:21.237
You will verify the package, configure the tenant, install the site, and then confirm that it is ready for users - not just that the scripts finished.

00:00:22.001 --> 00:00:27.647
Start with the release ZIP and the SHA256 receipt downloaded alongside it.

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:35.564
Run Get-FileHash with the SHA256 algorithm, and continue only when the calculated value matches the receipt.

00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:39.803
Extract the package into a new, empty install folder.

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:43.632
Then create a separate organization folder outside the kit.

00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:50.402
Keep the deployment settings and records there so replacing the kit will not overwrite them.

00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:58.867
Open Deployment-Settings.json in the organization folder, not the template inside the kit.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:06.812
Here, you are confirming the tenant name, SharePoint hosts, site alias, visibility, and security settings.

00:01:06.812 --> 00:01:11.058
For government content, set LearningEnvironment to Government.

00:01:11.858 --> 00:01:19.002
If you do not already have an approved provisioning app ID for this tenant, leave PnPClientID blank.

00:01:19.002 --> 00:01:22.440
script 01 will fill it in after registration.

00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:32.818
Next, add the organization's approved support and incident-reporting links, along with its governance links, training resources, and custom content.

00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:40.453
As each field appears on screen, confirm that it points to a route the responsible team owns and monitors.

00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:48.733
Before publishing, have those teams review the governance drafts, support routes, and organization-specific wording.

00:01:49.433 --> 00:01:53.997
From the kit folder, run the two preflight commands shown on screen.

00:01:54.797 --> 00:01:58.487
The first loads Internal\ContentPreflight.ps1.

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:04.795
The second checks the organization content, including the calendar format and required fields.

00:02:05.595 --> 00:02:09.353
Fix any reported issues before connecting to the tenant.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:14.267
Install PnP PowerShell version 3.2.0.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:26.538
If PnPClientID is blank because this tenant does not have an approved provisioning app, have someone who can grant tenant-wide admin consent run script 01.

00:02:27.338 --> 00:02:34.732
After registration, check that PnPClientID in the organization settings contains the app's client ID.

00:02:35.532 --> 00:02:41.130
Here in Entra, confirm that every required delegated permission shows as granted.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.210
Then open the Teams admin center.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:52.641
Confirm that Website, PDF, PowerPoint, and SharePoint pages and lists are available to the installer and intended users.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:58.835
Before you run anything, work out where the site should land.

00:02:58.835 --> 00:03:03.027
Combine SiteFQDN and MailNickname from the settings file.

00:03:03.027 --> 00:03:06.206
The resolved address format is shown on screen.

00:03:07.006 --> 00:03:11.333
Now run script 02 in customer mode with SeedDemoContent.

00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:16.676
That switch loads the site's pages, catalogs, calendar, and governance content.

00:03:17.476 --> 00:03:26.334
In the installer output, confirm the signed-in account, tenant, alias, owner, and target site address before resources are created.

00:03:27.134 --> 00:03:30.718
For a clean installation, do not use ResumeExisting.

00:03:30.718 --> 00:03:39.036
If an earlier attempt already created resources, stop and use the Failure and recovery boundary in the administrator guide.

00:03:41.306 --> 00:03:49.393
Now run Test-CoEInstall with the organization folder, site address, and the same ContentMode used for installation.

00:03:50.193 --> 00:03:51.484
Resolve every fail.

00:03:51.484 --> 00:03:56.105
Then read each warning and complete the manual review it identifies.

00:03:56.905 --> 00:04:06.351
Use a reader account to review the site, follow the support links, confirm the security configuration, and look for remaining demo content.

00:04:07.151 --> 00:04:10.617
Save the checker output in the organization folder.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:14.966
Passing the automated checks does not replace the manual review.

00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:20.768
To publish reviewed content changes, run script 03 with Scope All.

00:04:20.768 --> 00:04:25.599
Then run Test-CoEInstall again and repeat the relevant manual checks.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:30.022
RepairCapturedPages is not part of a routine update.

00:04:30.022 --> 00:04:36.463
Use it only when recovery work or checker results show that preserved managed pages need repair.

00:04:37.263 --> 00:04:44.980
The option can replace managed parts of Home and the captured pages, including changes made directly in SharePoint.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:49.274
Review what it will replace before using it on an existing site.

00:04:50.074 --> 00:04:56.381
Complete the handoff only when the checks pass and the required manual reviews are documented.

00:04:57.283 --> 00:05:03.446
Before handoff, remember that a clean checker run means the build matches the settings.

00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:08.830
It does not replace content, security, accessibility, or operational review.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:16.856
Keep the organization settings, deployment reports, logs, checker output, and review records together.

00:05:17.656 --> 00:05:23.606
For recovery or removal, use the administrator guide included with the same release.

